  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-15, on v0.21.0.\n\nHis words: \"everytime i move the mouse pointer the tool editor modal windoww changes its with until it fills the window\"\n\nWhat happens: the tool editor window becomes wider at each mouse move (each repaint). It stops when it fills the main window.\n\nExpected: the tool editor keeps its width between frames. It changes width only when the user drags its edge.\n\nProbable cause, not confirmed: an egui window whose content width comes from the available width of the previous frame (a full-width widget, a separator, `ui.available_width()` or a text field set to the full width inside an auto-sized window). Each frame then adds the margin to the width.\n\nFor the work:\n\n- Find the widget in the tool editor that sets its width from the window width. Name it in the PR.\n- Give the window a fixed default width or a max width, or give the widget a fixed width.\n- Check the other modal windows for the same pattern and name the result in the PR.\n\nDone means:\n\n- The tool editor width is the same after 100 frames with the pointer moving as after the first frame.\n- A UI test pins that width (a value test in the default ui suite, not a pixel snapshot).\n",
